;; spec:   stdlib §2.7 (print forms), tranche 2 plan C2-22 and D7 (Proposed)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  no implementation of Show for (Iterate i64)
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: iterate println
;; Proposed (plan recommendation, owner not yet confirmed; stdlib §8.2.1 item 14): Iterate, Repeat and Cycle have no
;; Show instance, so printing one is a compile error that names the type, where a print of an endless seq
;; would never return. (A bounded view is (println (vec (take 5 s))).) The instance would come with
;; `*print-length*` (tranche 5); the day it does this case is edited with the reason.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.print))

(defun main () -> i64
  (do (println (iterate inc 0))
      0))
